{"title":"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less than twice the square of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f823a6348af4c10de20f260b55360980673bc98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ -26 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 10 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 26 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 38 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"456\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The square of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e9136809f832318fdd66a5180d0e20660e072b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{2} = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />. Twice that would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less than that would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/1/3f1b53aa784c8b7b5a50182128c949fc384ca5e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32 - 6 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat\">1999 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b